{"info": {"total": 42, "parameters": {"skip": 0, "limit": 8, "q": "Chinese lady", "has_image": "1", "select": "accession_number,accession_number_sortable,cover_accession_number,department,collection,classification_type,gallery,department", "search": "Chinese lady"}}, "data": [{"id": 137121, "accession_number": "1961.89", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Lady Xuanwen Giving Instruction on the Rites of Zhou (\u5ba3\u6587\u541b\u6388\u7d93\u5716), 1638. Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; image: 172.8 x 55.7 cm (68 1/16 x 21 15/16 in.); overall: 293.9 x 71 cm (115 11/16 x 27 15/16 in.); with knobs: 293.9 x 79 cm (115 11/16 x 31 1/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund, 1961.89", "current_location": null, "title": "Lady Xuanwen Giving Instruction on the Rites of Zhou", "title_in_original_language": "\u5ba3\u6587\u541b\u6388\u7d93\u5716", "creation_date": "1638", "creation_date_earliest": 1638, "creation_date_latest": 1638, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Ming dynasty (1368\u20131644)"], "technique": "Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Hanging scroll", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Image: 172.8 x 55.7 cm (68 1/16 x 21 15/16 in.); Overall: 293.9 x 71 cm (115 11/16 x 27 15/16 in.); with knobs: 293.9 x 79 cm (115 11/16 x 31 1/8 in.)", "dimensions": {"image": {"height": 1.728, "height_inch": 68, "height_inch_fraction": 0.0625, "width": 0.557, "width_inch": 21, "width_inch_fraction": 0.9375}, "overall": {"height": 2.939, "height_inch": 115, "height_inch_fraction": 0.6875, "width": 0.71, "width_inch": 27, "width_inch_fraction": 0.9375}, "with knobs": {"height": 2.939, "height_inch": 115, "height_inch_fraction": 0.6875, "width": 0.79, "width_inch": 31, "width_inch_fraction": 0.125}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "\u5ba3\u6587\u541b\u8005\u97cb\u901e\u6bcd\u5b8b\u6c0f\u4e5f\u3002\u7236\u6388\u4ee5\u5468\u5b98\u97f3\u7fa9\uff0c\u66f0\uff1a\u543e\u5bb6\u4e16\u5b78\u50b3\u5468\u5b98\u3002\u50b3\u696d\u76f8\u7e7c\u3002\u6b64\u53c8\u5468\u516c\u6240\u88fd\uff0c\u7d93\u7d00\u3014\u5178\u3015\u8aa5\u767e\u5b98\u54c1\u7269\u5099\u65bc\u6b64\u77e3\u3002\u5973\u53ef\u53d7\u4e4b\u3002\u541b\u8af7\u8aa6\u4e0d\u8f1f\u3002\u77f3\u5e1d\u5f99\u5c71\u6771\u3002\u541b\u4e43\u63a8\u9e7f\u8eca\uff0c\u80cc\u8ca0\u7236\u6240\u6388\u66f8\u5230\u5180\u5dde\u3002\u901e\u6642\u5e74\u5c11\u3002\u665d\u5247\u63a1\u6a35\uff0c\u591c\u5247\u6559\u901e\u3002\u901e\u9042\u5b78\u6210\u540d\u7acb\u3002\u4ed5\u7b26\u5805\u70ba\u592a\u5e38\u3002\u5805\u5e38\u5e78\u5176\u592a\u5b78\uff0c\u554f\u535a\u58eb\u7d93\u5178\u3002\u4e43\u61ab\u79ae\u6a02\u907a\u7f3a\u3002\u6642\u535a\u58eb\u76e7\u58fa\u5c0d\u66f0\uff1a\u5ee2\u5b78\u65e2\u4e45\uff0c\u66f8\u50b3\u96f6\u843d\u3002\u6bd4\u5e74\u7db4\u64b0\uff0c\u6b63\u7d93\u7c97\u96c6\u3002\u60df\u5468\u5b98\u3001\u79ae\u7d93\uff0c\u672a\u6709\u5176\u5e2b\u3002\u7aca\u898b\u592a\u5e38\u97cb\u901e\u6bcd\u5b8b\u6c0f\u4e16\u5b78\u5bb6\uff0c\u5973\u50b3\u5176\u7236\u696d\u3002\u5f97\u5468\u5b98\u97f3\u7fa9\u3002\u4eca\u5e74\u516b\u5341\u3002\u8996\u807d\u7121\u95d5\u3002\u975e\u6b64\u6bcd\u7121\u53ef\u50b3\u6388\u5f8c\u751f\u3002\u4e8e\u662f\u5c31\u5b8b\u6c0f\u5bb6\u7acb\u8b1b\u5802\uff0c\u7f6e\u751f\u54e1\u767e\u4e8c\u5341\u4eba\u3002\u9694\u7d73\u7d17\u7e35\u800c\u6388\u696d\u7109\u3002\u62dc\u5b8b\u6c0f\u7235\uff0c\u865f\u70ba\u5ba3\u6587\u541b\u3002\u8cdc\u4f8d\u5a62\u5341\u4eba\u3002\u5468\u5b98\u5b78\u5f8c\u884c\u4e8e\u4e16\u3002\n\n\u5d07\u798e\u620a\u5bc5\u516b\u6708\u4e8c\u65e5\uff0c\u70ba\u7dac\u59d1\u516d\u65ec\u4e4b\u8fb0\u3002\u7dac\u5f1f\u81ea\u6210\u70ba\u59d1\u5066\u3002\u5055\u59d1\u5b63\u5973\u99f1\u5bc6\u3001\u5916\u5b6b\u6979\u3001\u6960\u3001\u6969\u3001\u6a52\u3001\u695e\u3001\u68c5\u3001\u5b6b\u5973\u60e0\u3001\u6f09\u9152\u4e0a\u58fd\uff0c\u5c6c\u7dac\u5716\u5beb\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5\u980c\u795d\u8005\u3002\u7dac\u601d\u5b8b\u6bcd\u5c1a\u4e94\u80e1\u4e4b\u6642\uff0c\u7d93\u85c9\u5c6c\u4e4b\u5a66\u4eba\uff1b\u4eca\u592a\u5e73\u6709\u8c61\uff0c\u800c\u79c9\u6756\u540d\u7fa9\u8005\uff0c\u7368\u7dac\u59d1\u723e\u3002\u656c\u5beb\u6b64\u5716\uff0c\u4e14\u539a\u671b\u4e8e\u5f1f\u7d39\u7109\u3002\u7336\u5b50\u6d2a\u7dac\u4e5d\u9813\u9996\u3002", "inscription_translation": "Artist's inscription and signature: \n\nLady Xuanwen is Wei Cheng\u2019s mother, nee Song. Her father transmitted to her the text, Zhou guan ying yi [The phonetics and meanings of the Rites of Zhou], and told her thus: \u201cIt is our family\u2019s tradition to uphold and continue the Zhou guan from one generation to the next. In addition, this text was written by the Duke of Zhou; it contains classics, annals, laws, titles, all officials and numerous things. It is your duty to receive it.\u201d Lady [Xuanwen] studied and recited the book without cease. Emperor Shi [Shi Fu \u77f3\u864e, 295\u2013349] moved his capital to Shandong. As a consequence, Lady followed suit by pushing a deer cart while carrying the manuscript from her father on her back. Wei Cheng at the time was a mere child. Consequently Lady gathered firewood during the day and taught Wei Cheng at nights. It came to pass that Wei Cheng became erudite, gained fame, and served as chamberlain for ceremonials under Fu Jian. Fu Jian often visited the National University. While raising questions about the [current state of] classics to those erudites, he lamented the losses of such texts regarding rites and music. One of those erudites, Lu Hu, responded: \u201cSuch matters have been laid waste for some time. Their transmissions were in fragments. In successive years, we have compiled a rough compendium of all classics. The only missing piece is Zhou guan, for which we do not have an instructor. Now it comes to my attention that Madam Song, the mother of Wei Cheng, the chamberlain for ceremonials, is from a family of scholars; she [is a rarity] of a woman who carried on her father\u2019s learning and is well versed in Zhou guan ying yi. She now is in her eightieth year, and is deficient in neither seeing nor hearing. Except for her, there is no one who could take on this duty for instructing the young.\u201d As a result, it was decided to erect a lecture hall in Madame Song\u2019s mansion, while recruiting and placing under her care a total of 120 younger scholars. By setting up a red gauze curtain [separating herself from her students], she began the instruction. \n\nOn this second day of the eighth month, the year of wuyin of the Chongzhen era [1638], is the birthday of my aunt. My cousin Zicheng is her son-in-law. He, together with my aunt\u2019s second daughter, Luomi, also the maternal grandsons Ying, Nan, Bian, Yun, Leng, Bing, and granddaughter Hui, poured wine to honor the birthday lady. In addition, it was their request that I should make a painting to celebrate the occasion. I have thought that Madame Song lived during the time when the Five Barbarian Tribes were holding sway and the classics were being assigned to women. Now is the time of peace; it is rare to see women [wise enough to] uphold correctness in titles and ranks, except for my aunt. Thereupon, I respectfully painted this picture, while also placing my earnest anticipation for [great deeds] from my cousin and his offspring. Your nephew, Hongshou, bows his head nine times.", "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"inscription": "5 additional seals: \n\n2 of Xu Weiren \u5f90\u6e2d\u4ec1(1788\uff0d1855); \n2 of Sun Zutong \u5b6b\u7956\u540c (1894\u20131937); \n1 of C. C. Wang \u738b\u5b63\u9077 (1907\u20132003).", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 2}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 302039, "title": "Year in Review (1961)", "description": "<i>Year in Review (1961)</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (November 1-26, 1961).", "opening_date": "1961-11-01T05:00:00"}, {"id": 516263, "title": "Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</i>. The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (organizer) (March 23-May 28, 1967); Los Angeles County Museum of Art, Los Angeles, CA (June 20-August 13, 1967); Fine Arts Museums of San Francisco, de Young Museum, San Francisco, CA (September 15-November 5, 1967).", "opening_date": "1967-03-24T05:00:00"}, {"id": 211775, "title": "Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art", "description": "<i>Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art</i>. Nara National Museum (organizer) (February 21-March 29, 1998); Suntory Museum of Art (April 28-June 21, 1998).", "opening_date": "1998-02-21T00:00:00"}, {"id": 539332, "title": "Six Dynasties of Chinese Painting (Chinese art rotation)", "description": "<i>Six Dynasties of Chinese Painting (Chinese art rotation)</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (November 10, 2023-May 5, 2024).", "opening_date": "2023-11-10T05:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</em>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 10-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982); The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (December 3, 1982-February 28, 1983).", "opening_date": "1980-11-06T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 119)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (July 16-October 28, 2003).", "opening_date": "2003-07-16T04:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 242)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (November 21, 2013-July 28, 2014).", "opening_date": "2013-11-21T05:00:00Z"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Wan Chengzi \u842c\u627f\u7d2b [1775\u2013after 1837]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "Xu Weiren \u5f90\u6e2d\u4ec1 [1788\u20131853]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "Sun Zutong \u5b6b\u7956\u540c [1894\u20131937]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "early 20th century", "sortorder": 3}, {"description": "(C. C. Wang \u738b\u5b63\u9077 [1907\u20132003], New York, NY,  sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131961", "sortorder": 4}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1961\u2013", "sortorder": 5}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "Chen Hongshou's long inscription at the top of the painting compares his virtuous aunt with the historical exemplar, Lady Xuanwen.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "This painting by Chen Hongshou depicts the story of Xuanwen Jun, or Lady of Literary Propagation, at a venerable age, instructing young scholars on the Confucian classics. It was painted for Chen\u2019s aunt in celebration of her 60th birthday. <br> <br>Chen\u2019s painting style is archaic in the use of fine outlines and brilliant coloring with mineral pigments. In depicting the figures, he uses the \u201ciron-wire\u201d brush style (fine, even lines) with deliberate control. The faces are elongated and exaggerated. A few ritual bronzes lend the scene an antique flavor.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60466052"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1961.89-lady-xuanwen-giving"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "Ho, Wai-Kam. \u201cNan-Ch\u2019en Pei-Ts\u2019ui: Ch\u2019en of the South and Ts\u2019ui of the North.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 49, no. 1 (1962): 1\u201311.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 1\u20138, Cover, figs. 1\u20133", "url": "http://www.jstor.org/stable/25142485"}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1966</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1966.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 265", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1966/page/n289"}, {"citation": "Cahill, James, and Virginia Field. <em>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</em>. [New York]: Asia Society; distributed by Abrams, 1967.", "page_number": "Reproduced: cat. no. 8", "url": null}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1969</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1969.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 265", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1969/page/n289"}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1978</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1978.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 352", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1978/page/n372"}, {"citation": "Ho, Wai-kam, Sherman E. Lee, Laurence Sickman, and Marc F. Wilson. <em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting: The Collections of the Nelson Gallery-Atkins Museum, Kansas City, and the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, in cooperation with Indiana University Press, 1980.", "page_number": "Reproduced:  pp. 272-273, cat. no. 208", "url": null}, {"citation": "<em>T\u014dy\u014d kaiga no seika: tokubetsuten: Kur\u012bvurando Bijutsukan no korekushon kara</em> [\u6771\u6d0b\u7d75\u753b\u306e\u7cbe\u83ef: \u7279\u522b\u5c55: \u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30f4\u30e9\u30f3\u30c8\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306e\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u304b\u3089 = Highlights of Asian painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art]. Japan: Nara National Museum, 1998.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pp. 66-67, cat. no. 41", "url": null}, {"citation": "Yang, Kathleen \u694a\u51f1\u7433, and Chi-ch\u02bbien Wang \u738b\u5b63\u9077. <em>Through a Chinese connoisseur's eye: private notes of C.C. Wang</em> \u738b\u5b63\u9077\u8b80\u66f8\u7b46\u8a18. Beijing: Zhong hua shu ju, 2010.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: p. 312, no. 32", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>The CMA Companion: A Guide to the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland: Cleveland Museum of Art, 2014.", "page_number": "Mentioned and reproduced: P. 108", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Chou, Ju-hsi and Anita Chung. <em>Silent Poetry: Chinese Paintings from the Collection of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, 2015.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 314\u2013320", "url": null}, {"citation": "Vinograd, Richard. \"Composite Identities: Portraits.\" In <em>Repentant Monk: Illusion and Disillusion in the Art of Chen Hongshou. </em>Julia M. White, ed., 57-67. Oakland, California: University of California Press, 2017.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 59, fig. 5.2", "url": null}, {"citation": "Vinograd, Richard Ellis. <em>Facing China: Truth and Memory in Portraiture</em>. London: Reaktion Books, 2022.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: p. 246, fig. 128", "url": ""}, {"citation": "\"Permanent Collection Installations: Six Dynasties of Chinese Paintings.\u201d <em>Cleveland Art: Cleveland Museum of Art Members Magazine </em>63, no. 4 (2023): 18\u201319.", "page_number": "Reproduced and Mentioned: p. 19", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAMM2023-04/page/18/mode/2up"}, {"citation": "Burnett, Katharine. \"Weirder than Weird : 'Weird Figure' Painting of Luohans and Literati in Seventeenth-Century China.\" <em>Artibus Asiae </em>84, n. 1 (2024): 81\u2013109.", "page_number": "Mentioned: p. 108; Reproduced: p. 104, fig. 19.", "url": ""}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1961.89", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_web.jpg", "width": "307", "height": "893", "filesize": "228678", "filename": "1961.89_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_print.jpg", "width": "1167", "height": "3400", "filesize": "3308808", "filename": "1961.89_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_full.tif", "width": "2187", "height": "6370", "filesize": "41820400", "filename": "1961.89_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "726", "height": "900", "filesize": "229302"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "2743", "height": "3400", "filesize": "3653367"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt0_full.tif", "width": "5911", "height": "7328", "filesize": "129977668"}, "date_created": "2015-05-05T11:43:24", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt1_web.jpg", "width": "251", "height": "893", "filesize": "162588"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt1_print.jpg", "width": "955", "height": "3400", "filesize": "2333375"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt1_full.tif", "width": "1796", "height": "6391", "filesize": "34460956"}, "date_created": "2010-02-22T18:14:40", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt2_web.jpg", "width": "1076", "height": "893", "filesize": "706580"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt2_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2823", "filesize": "8307716"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt2_full.tif", "width": "6012", "height": "4992", "filesize": "90064524"}, "date_created": "2010-02-22T18:51:33", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt3_web.jpg", "width": "1193", "height": "893", "filesize": "851351"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt3_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2545", "filesize": "8005358"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt3_full.tif", "width": "6668", "height": "4992", "filesize": "99888872"}, "date_created": "2010-02-22T18:59:03", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt4_web.jpg", "width": "1193", "height": "893", "filesize": "793790"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt4_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2545", "filesize": "7713674"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt4_full.tif", "width": "6668", "height": "4992", "filesize": "99888380"}, "date_created": "2010-02-22T19:05:18", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt5_web.jpg", "width": "327", "height": "893", "filesize": "236806"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt5_print.jpg", "width": "1244", "height": "3400", "filesize": "3283366"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt5_full.tif", "width": "2470", "height": "6752", "filesize": "50054060"}, "date_created": "2009-12-08T23:08:38", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt6_web.jpg", "width": "1263", "height": "886", "filesize": "889462"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt6_print.jpg", "width": "3080", "height": "2160", "filesize": "5892058"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt6_full.tif", "width": "3080", "height": "2160", "filesize": "19980164"}, "date_created": "2009-12-08T23:08:56", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt7_web.jpg", "width": "975", "height": "893", "filesize": "736978"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt7_print.jpg", "width": "2768", "height": "2536", "filesize": "5621137"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt7_full.tif", "width": "2768", "height": "2536", "filesize": "21080156"}, "date_created": "2009-12-08T23:09:10", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt8_web.jpg", "width": "612", "height": "893", "filesize": "414112"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt8_print.jpg", "width": "2144", "height": "3128", "filesize": "4956694"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt8_full.tif", "width": "2144", "height": "3128", "filesize": "20140508"}, "date_created": "2009-12-08T23:09:23", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt9_web.jpg", "width": "286", "height": "893", "filesize": "54729"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt9_print.jpg", "width": "492", "height": "1536", "filesize": "164322"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1961.89/1961.89_alt9_full.tif", "width": "492", "height": "1536", "filesize": "167998"}, "annotation": ""}], "creditline": "Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 137121, "creators": [{"id": 6274, "description": "Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": "\u9673\u6d2a\u7dac", "birth_year": "1598", "death_year": "1652", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1961-05-01T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1638, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1638", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "object", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": ["Lady Xuanwen Jun Giving Instructions on the Classics", "Lady Xuanwen Jun Giving Instructions on the Rites of Zhou", "Lady Xuanwen Giving Instruction on the Rites of Zhou \u5ba3\u6587\u541b\u6388\u7d93\u5716", "Lady Hs\u00fcan-wen Giving Instructions on the Classics"], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-06-19 11:13:35.408000"}, {"id": 149603, "accession_number": "1979.27", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Paintings after Ancient Masters (\u8001\u84ee\u6a45\u53e4), 1598\u20131652. Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652). Double album with twenty-two leaves; ink or ink and color on silk; overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1979.27", "current_location": null, "title": "Paintings after Ancient Masters", "title_in_original_language": "\u8001\u84ee\u6a45\u53e4", "creation_date": "1598\u20131652", "creation_date_earliest": 1598, "creation_date_latest": 1652, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Ming dynasty (1368\u20131644)"], "technique": "Double album with twenty-two leaves; ink or ink and color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Album leaf", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.)", "dimensions": {"sheet": {"height": 0.242, "height_inch": 9, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.237, "width_inch": 9, "width_inch_fraction": 0.3125}, "overall": {"height": 0.302, "height_inch": 11, "height_inch_fraction": 0.875, "width": 0.267, "width_inch": 10, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}, "cover": {"height": 0.305, "height_inch": 12, "height_inch_fraction": 0.0, "width": 0.267, "width_inch": 10, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "Artist's titles, signatures, and 21 seals:\n\nA. Scholars in a Garden.  Hung-shou painted for old Chung. [seal] Chang-hou.\nB. Lao-tzu Riding an Ox.  Hung-shou respectfully painted. [seal] Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nC. Narcissus and Bare Trees. The Taoist Chung-ch'ing entrusted Lao-lien to paint [this]. [seal] Chang-hou.\nD. Autumn Landscape. Lao-lien painted this for Lao-ts'ang. [seal] Chang-hou.\nE. Portrait of T'ao Yuan-ming. Lao-lien [seal] Hung-shou.\nF. Lotus and Rocks. Hung-shou painted after the style of Ts'ui Po and presented it to the Buddhist disciple Lin Chung-ch'ing. [seal] Chang-hou.\nG. Taoist and Crane in Autumn Landscape. The old man Fu-ch'ih painted for the Taoist Chung-ch'ing. [seal] Chang-hou.\nH. Portrait of Chung-ch'ing in a Landscape. Lao-lien painted for Chung-ch'ing. [2 seals] Chang-hou; Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nI. Chrysanthemum and Rock. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.\nJ. Landscape in the Style of Ni Tsan. Lao-lien [seal] Chang-hou.\nL. Mr. Five Willows (Wu-liu), T'ao Yung-ming. Mr. Five Willows Chung-ch'ing entrusted Hung-shou to paint [this]. [seal] Chang-hou.\nM. A Lohan [after Kuan-hsui]. Buddhist disciple Ch'en Hung-shou respectfully painted. [2 seals] Chun-t'i ti-tzu; Chang-hou.\nN. A Bird and Peach-Blossom Branch. Hui-lun-shang painted after Tao-chun [Emperor Hui-tsung] and presented it to Ts'ang-fu chu-chih. [seal] Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nO. Travellers in an Autumn Landscape. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nP. A Lady. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.\nQ. Crysanthemum. Hung-shou painted in imitation of the Northern Sung style for Taoist friend, Ts'ang-fu. [seal] Chang-hou.\nR. Scholar Reading in a Thatched Hut by a Waterfall. Chung-ch'ing entrusted Hung-shou to paint. [seal] Chang-hou.\nS. Scholar with Staff and Brush. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nT. An Ancient Tree. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nU. Rock, Old Tree, and Bamboo. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}, {"inscription": "2 colophons (leaves K and V) and 34 additional seals:  24 seals of Lin Chung-ch'ing (Lin Ts'ang-fu or Lin T'ing-tung, friend of Chen Hongshou, for whom the album was painted); 2 colophons, dated 1893 and 1899, and 5 seals of Weng Tonghe \u7fc1\u540c\u9fa2 (1830-1904); 2 seals of Weng Tongjue \u7fc1\u540c\u7235 (older brother of Weng Tonghe; 1814-1877); 2 seals of Weng Wan-go \u7fc1\u842c\u6208 (1918-2020); 1 unidentified.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 304412, "title": "Year in Review: 1979", "description": "<i>Year in Review: 1979</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (organizer) (February 13-March 9, 1980).", "opening_date": "1980-02-13T05:00:00"}, {"id": 304517, "title": "Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</i>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 11-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982); The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (December 3, 1982-February 28, 1983).", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T05:00:00"}, {"id": 309887, "title": "The Twain Shall Meet", "description": "<i>The Twain Shall Meet</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (October 30, 1985-January 5, 1986).", "opening_date": "1985-10-30T05:00:00"}, {"id": 310119, "title": "Realm of the Immortals: Daoism in the Arts of China", "description": "<i>Realm of the Immortals: Daoism in the Arts of China</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (February 10-April 10, 1988).", "opening_date": "1988-02-10T05:00:00"}, {"id": 311446, "title": "Asian Autumn: Masterpieces from the Collection", "description": "<i>Asian Autumn: Masterpieces from the Collection</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (September 17, 1991-January 5, 1992).", "opening_date": "1991-09-17T04:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Five centuries of Chinese painting: Ming &amp; Ch'ing dynasties. </em>Dallas Museum of Fine Arts, Dallas, TX (June 27\u2013August 8, 1954).", "opening_date": "1954-06-27T04:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>1000 Jahre Chinesische Malerei</em>. Haus der Kunst, Munich, Germany (October 16-December 13, 1959).", "opening_date": "1959-10-16T04:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Chinese Art: An Exhibition of Paintings, Jades, Bronzes and Ceramics: Being a Contribution Made by Smith College Museum of Art to the College Interim Session, 1962</em>. Northampton, MA (1962). (leaves A-J)", "opening_date": "1962-01-01T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Fantastics and Eccentrics</em>. Asia House Gallery, New York, NY, (March 23-May 28, 1967); Los Angeles County Museum of Art, CA (June 20-August 13, 1967); and M. H. De Young Memorial Museum, San Francisco, CA (September 15-November 5, 1967).", "opening_date": "1967-03-23T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Chinese Painting from the Two Distinguished American Museums</em>. Tokyo National Museum, Tokyo, Japan (October 4-November 17,1982).", "opening_date": "1982-10-04T04:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Nara National Museum (organizer) (February 21-March 29, 1998); Suntory Museum of Art (April 28-June 21, 1998).", "opening_date": "1998-02-21T05:00:00Z"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Weng Tonghe \u7fc1\u540c\u9fa2 [1830\u20131904], by descent to  Wango H. C. Weng", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "(Wango H. C. Weng \u7fc1\u842c\u6208 [1918\u20132020], Lyme, NH, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "?\u20131979", "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "1979\u2013", "sortorder": 3}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "Chen Hongshou made this double album with twenty paintings for a friend, Lin Zhongqing.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "The twenty paintings in this double album by Chen Hongshou include landscapes, figures, and flowers. It also has one leaf featuring a woman, an often-used subject not found in the other albums from the latter part of his career. His late works are wonderful summations of Chen's peculiar and quirky art\u2014archaistic, hyper-refined\u2014but without accompanying shallowness or sentimentality.<br><br>His figures and landscapes in the late albums are miniaturized, not unlike the small Chinese gardens, or the carefully selected small table rocks or old roots used for contemplation to see the world in miniature. This loss of scale is quite deliberate and reflects the psychological situation of a depressed class like the Ming loyalist officials and scholars, deprived of their integrity and honor, and forced to lead a diminished and restricted existence.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60473781"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1979.27-paintings-after-anci"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "<em>Five Centuries of Chinese Painting: Ming &amp; Ch'ing Dynasties : [Exhibition] June 27 Through August 8, 1954, Dallas Museum of Fine Arts</em>. Dallas: Dallas Museum of Fine Arts, 1954.", "page_number": "cat. no. 24", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Goepper, Roger. <em>1000 Jahre chinesische Malerei</em>. Mu\u0308nchen: Haus der Kunst, 1959.", "page_number": "cat. no. 81", "url": ""}, {"citation": "<em>Chinese Art: An Exhibition of Paintings, Jades, Bronzes and Ceramics</em>. Northampton, MA: Smith College Museum of Art, 1962.", "page_number": "cat. no. 25", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Cahill, James, and Virginia Field. <em>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</em>. [New York]: Asia Society; distributed by Abrams, 1967.", "page_number": "pp. 38, 39, cat. no. 10", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Lee, Sherman E. \"The Year in Review for 1979.\" <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 67, no. 3 (1980): 58-99.", "page_number": "Mentioned: cat. no. 112, p. 62, 98", "url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/25159667"}, {"citation": "Ho, Wai-kam, Sherman E. Lee, Laurence Sickman, and Marc F. Wilson. <em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting: The Collections of the Nelson Gallery-Atkins Museum, Kansas City, and the Cleveland Museum of Art.</em> Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, in cooperation with Indiana University Press, 1980.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: cat. no. 207, pp. 268\u2013272", "url": null}, {"citation": "<em>T\u014dy\u014d kaiga no seika: tokubetsuten: Kur\u012bvurando Bijutsukan no korekushon kara </em>[\u6771\u6d0b\u7d75\u753b\u306e\u7cbe\u83ef: \u7279\u522b\u5c55: \u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30f4\u30e9\u30f3\u30c8\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306e\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u304b\u3089= Highlights of Asian painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art]. Nara, Japan: Nara National Museum, 1998.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 68\u201369, cat. no. 42", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Chou, Ju-hsi and Anita Chung. <em>Silent poetry: Chinese paintings from the collection of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 2015.", "page_number": "Mentioned: p. 314", "url": ""}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1979.27", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27/1979.27_web.jpg", "width": "759", "height": "900", "filesize": "211631", "filename": "1979.27_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27/1979.27_print.jpg", "width": "2868", "height": "3400", "filesize": "2577503", "filename": "1979.27_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27/1979.27_full.tif", "width": "3870", "height": "4588", "filesize": "53292020", "filename": "1979.27_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [], "creditline": "John L. Severance Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 149603, "creators": [{"id": 6274, "description": "Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": "\u9673\u6d2a\u7dac", "birth_year": "1598", "death_year": "1652", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1979-06-21T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1598, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1598\u20131652", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "cover", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-05-29 07:42:18.131000"}, {"id": 151414, "accession_number": "1983.25", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Court Lady with High Chignon, c. 700\u2013750. North China, Tang dynasty (618-907). Earthenware with polychromy; overall: 31.6 cm (12 7/16 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund, 1983.25", "current_location": "239 Chinese Ceramics and Metalwork", "title": "Court Lady with High Chignon", "creation_date": "c. 700\u2013750", "creation_date_earliest": 700, "creation_date_latest": 750, "artists_tags": [], "culture": ["North China, Tang dynasty (618-907)"], "technique": "earthenware with polychromy", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "China - Tang Dynasty", "type": "Sculpture", "measurements": "Overall: 31.6 cm (12 7/16 in.)", "dimensions": {"overall": {"height": 0.316, "height_inch": 12, "height_inch_fraction": 0.4375}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 309669, "title": "The Year in Review for 1983", "description": "<i>The Year in Review for 1983</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (February 22-April 8, 1984).", "opening_date": "1984-02-22T05:00:00"}], "legacy": []}, "provenance": [{"description": "(Osborne I. Hauge [1913\u20132004] and Victor Lloyd Hauge [1919\u20132013], Falls Church, VA, sold to  the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131983", "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1983\u2013", "sortorder": 2}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "Tang aristocratic women had a high degree of freedom, especially in contrast with the Neo-Confucianism of the later Song dynasty.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "Tang figurines placed in the tombs give a vivid picture of everyday life. Images of elegant ladies in various hairstyles, costumes, and activities suggest the fashion of the time. This slender court woman's clasped hands are covered by long, narrow sleeves. Her v-neck blouse is tucked into a floor-length skirt with empire waistband. A long stole drawn from the bodice and across the back falls between her wrists. Her skirt is painted with thin red stripes, the waistband with double red circles, and the stole with white rosettes in unfired pigments. Her black hair is piled into high angled chignon.<br><br>Together with other figurines\u2014court officials, musicians, dancers, hunters, foreign travelers, horses, camels, guardian warriors, and guardian animals\u2014such tomb sculptures accompanied the deceased in the afterlife.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60762460"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1983.25-court-lady-with-high"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "Turner, Evan H. \u201cYear in Review for 1983.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 71, no. 2 (1984): 38\u201379.", "page_number": "Mentioned: p. 77, no. 244", "url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/25159848"}, {"citation": "Neils, Jenifer. \u201cThe Twain Shall Meet.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>, vol. 72, no. 6, 1985, pp. 326\u2013359.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 346, fig. 38", "url": "https://www.jstor.org/stable/25159914"}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1983.25", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_web.jpg", "width": "655", "height": "893", "filesize": "47071", "filename": "1983.25_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_print.jpg", "width": "2494", "height": "3400", "filesize": "616147", "filename": "1983.25_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_full.tif", "width": "5019", "height": "6841", "filesize": "103036472", "filename": "1983.25_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "641", "height": "893", "filesize": "46860"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "2442", "height": "3400", "filesize": "631597"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1983.25/1983.25_alt0_full.tif", "width": "4903", "height": "6824", "filesize": "100404436"}, "date_created": "2012-08-28T17:16:21", "annotation": ""}], "creditline": "Severance and Greta Millikin Purchase Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 151414, "creators": [], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1983-03-07T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 700, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "c. 700\u2013750", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "object", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-07-17 11:04:03.223000"}, {"id": 149616, "accession_number": "1979.27.2", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Paintings after Ancient Masters: Volume 2 (\u8001\u84ee\u6a45\u53e4), 1598\u20131652. Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652). Album with eleven leaves; ink or ink and color on silk; overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1979.27.2", "current_location": null, "title": "Paintings after Ancient Masters: Volume 2", "title_in_original_language": "\u8001\u84ee\u6a45\u53e4", "creation_date": "1598\u20131652", "creation_date_earliest": 1598, "creation_date_latest": 1652, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Ming dynasty (1368\u20131644)"], "technique": "Album with eleven leaves; ink or ink and color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Album leaf", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.)", "dimensions": {"painting only": {"height": 0.242, "height_inch": 9, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.237, "width_inch": 9, "width_inch_fraction": 0.3125}, "overall": {"height": 0.302, "height_inch": 11, "height_inch_fraction": 0.875, "width": 0.267, "width_inch": 10, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}, "cover": {"height": 0.305, "height_inch": 12, "height_inch_fraction": 0.0, "width": 0.267, "width_inch": 10, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "Artist's titles, signatures, and 21 seals:\n\nA. Scholars in a Garden.  Hung-shou painted for old Chung. [seal] Chang-hou.\nB. Lao-tzu Riding an Ox.  Hung-shou respectfully painted. [seal] Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nC. Narcissus and Bare Trees. The Taoist Chung-ch'ing entrusted Lao-lien to paint [this]. [seal] Chang-hou.\nD. Autumn Landscape. Lao-lien painted this for Lao-ts'ang. [seal] Chang-hou.\nE. Portrait of T'ao Yuan-ming. Lao-lien [seal] Hung-shou.\nF. Lotus and Rocks. Hung-shou painted after the style of Ts'ui Po and presented it to the Buddhist disciple Lin Chung-ch'ing. [seal] Chang-hou.\nG. Taoist and Crane in Autumn Landscape. The old man Fu-ch'ih painted for the Taoist Chung-ch'ing. [seal] Chang-hou.\nH. Portrait of Chung-ch'ing in a Landscape. Lao-lien painted for Chung-ch'ing. [2 seals] Chang-hou; Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nI. Chrysanthemum and Rock. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.\nJ. Landscape in the Style of Ni Tsan. Lao-lien [seal] Chang-hou.\nL. Mr. Five Willows (Wu-liu), T'ao Yung-ming. Mr. Five Willows Chung-ch'ing entrusted Hung-shou to paint [this]. [seal] Chang-hou.\nM. A Lohan [after Kuan-hsui]. Buddhist disciple Ch'en Hung-shou respectfully painted. [2 seals] Chun-t'i ti-tzu; Chang-hou.\nN. A Bird and Peach-Blossom Branch. Hui-lun-shang painted after Tao-chun [Emperor Hui-tsung] and presented it to Ts'ang-fu chu-chih. [seal] Ch'en yin Hung-shou.\nO. Travellers in an Autumn Landscape. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nP. A Lady. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.\nQ. Crysanthemum. Hung-shou painted in imitation of the Northern Sung style for Taoist friend, Ts'ang-fu. [seal] Chang-hou.\nR. Scholar Reading in a Thatched Hut by a Waterfall. Chung-ch'ing entrusted Hung-shou to paint. [seal] Chang-hou.\nS. Scholar with Staff and Brush. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nT. An Ancient Tree. Hung-shou [seal] Chang-hou.\nU. Rock, Okd Tree, and Bamboo. Hung-shou [seal] Hung-shou.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}, {"inscription": "2 colophons (leaves K and V) and 34 additional seals:  24 seals of Lin Chung-ch'ing (Lin Ts'ang-fu or Lin T'ing-tung, friend of Chen Hongshou, for whom the album was painted); 2 colophons, dated 1893 and 1899, and 5 seals of Weng Tonghe \u7fc1\u540c\u9fa2 (1830-1904); 2 seals of Weng Tongjue \u7fc1\u540c\u7235 (older brother of Weng Tonghe; 1814-1877); 2 seals of Weng Wan-go \u7fc1\u842c\u6208 (1918-2020); 1 unidentified.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 304517, "title": "Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</i>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 11-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982); The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (December 3, 1982-February 28, 1983).", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T05:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Five centuries of Chinese painting: Ming &amp; Ch'ing dynasties. </em>Dallas Museum of Fine Arts, Dallas, TX (June 27\u2013August 8, 1954).", "opening_date": "1954-08-08T00:00:00"}, {"description": "<em>1000 Jahre Chinesische Malerei</em>. Haus der Kunst, Munich, Germany (October 16-December 13, 1959).", "opening_date": "1959-10-16T00:00:00"}, {"description": "<em>Chinese Art: An Exhibition of Paintings, Jades, Bronzes and Ceramics: Being a Contribution Made by Smith College Museum of Art to the College Interim Session, 1962</em>. Northampton, MA (1962). (leaves A-J)", "opening_date": "1962-01-01T00:00:00"}, {"description": "<em>Fantastics and Eccentrics</em>. Asia House Gallery, New York, NY, (March 23-May 28, 1967); Los Angeles County Museum of Art, CA (June 20-August 13, 1967); and M. H. De Young Memorial Museum, San Francisco, CA (September 15-November 5, 1967).", "opening_date": "1967-03-23T00:00:00"}, {"description": "<em>Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Nara National Museum (organizer) (February 21-March 29, 1998); Suntory Museum of Art (April 28-June 21, 1998).", "opening_date": "1998-02-21T00:00:00"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Weng Tonghe \u7fc1\u540c\u9fa2 [1830\u20131904], by descent to  Wango H. C. Weng", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "(Wango H. C. Weng \u7fc1\u842c\u6208 [1918\u20132020], Lyme, NH, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "?\u20131979", "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "1979\u2013", "sortorder": 3}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": ["79.27k-u"], "did_you_know": "This album was treasured by 5 generations of the Weng family, from imperial tutor Weng Tonghe (1830\u20131904) through Wango Weng (1918\u20132020), an art historian, connoisseur, and filmmaker.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "The twenty paintings in this double album by Chen Hongshou include landscapes, figures, and flowers. It also has one leaf featuring a woman, an often-used subject not found in the other albums from the latter part of his career. His late works are wonderful summations of Chen's peculiar and quirky art\u2014archaistic, hyper-refined\u2014but without accompanying shallowness or sentimentality.<br><br>His figures and landscapes in the late albums are miniaturized, not unlike the small Chinese gardens, or the carefully selected small table rocks or old roots used for contemplation to see the world in miniature. This loss of scale is quite deliberate and reflects the psychological situation of a depressed class like the Ming loyalist officials and scholars, deprived of their integrity and honor, and forced to lead a diminished and restricted existence.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60473841"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1979.27.2-paintings-after-anci"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "<em>Five Centuries of Chinese Painting: Ming &amp; Ch'ing Dynasties : [Exhibition] June 27 Through August 8, 1954, Dallas Museum of Fine Arts</em>. Dallas: Dallas Museum of Fine Arts, 1954.", "page_number": "cat. no. 24", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Goepper, Roger. <em>1000 Jahre chinesische Malerei</em>. Mu\u0308nchen: Haus der Kunst, 1959.", "page_number": "cat. no. 81", "url": ""}, {"citation": "<em>Chinese Art: An Exhibition of Paintings, Jades, Bronzes and Ceramics</em>. Northampton, MA: Smith College Museum of Art, 1962.", "page_number": "cat. no. 25", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Cahill, James, and Virginia Field. <em>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</em>. [New York]: Asia Society; distributed by Abrams, 1967.", "page_number": "pp. 38, 39, cat. no. 10", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Ho, Wai-kam, Sherman E. Lee, Laurence Sickman, and Marc F. Wilson. <em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting: The Collections of the Nelson Gallery-Atkins Museum, Kansas City, and the Cleveland Museum of Art.</em> Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, in cooperation with Indiana University Press, 1980.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: cat. no. 207, pp. 268\u2013272", "url": ""}, {"citation": "<em>T\u014dy\u014d kaiga no seika: tokubetsuten: Kur\u012bvurando Bijutsukan no korekushon kara </em>[\u6771\u6d0b\u7d75\u753b\u306e\u7cbe\u83ef: \u7279\u522b\u5c55: \u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30f4\u30e9\u30f3\u30c8\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306e\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u304b\u3089= Highlights of Asian painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art]. Nara, Japan: Nara National Museum, 1998.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 68\u201369, cat. no. 42", "url": ""}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1979.27.2", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2/1979.27.2_web.jpg", "width": "800", "height": "893", "filesize": "477315", "filename": "1979.27.2_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2/1979.27.2_print.jpg", "width": "3045", "height": "3400", "filesize": "7036154", "filename": "1979.27.2_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2/1979.27.2_full.tif", "width": "4770", "height": "5326", "filesize": "76242636", "filename": "1979.27.2_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [], "creditline": "John L. Severance Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 149616, "creators": [{"id": 6274, "description": "Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": "\u9673\u6d2a\u7dac", "birth_year": "1598", "death_year": "1652", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1979-06-21T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1598, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1598\u20131652", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "component", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": "1979.27", "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-05-29 07:42:22.884000"}, {"id": 149621, "accession_number": "1979.27.2.16", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Paintings after Ancient Masters: A Lady, 1598\u20131652. Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652). Album leaf, ink and color on silk; overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1979.27.2.16", "current_location": null, "title": "Paintings after Ancient Masters: A Lady", "creation_date": "1598\u20131652", "creation_date_earliest": 1598, "creation_date_latest": 1652, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Ming dynasty (1368\u20131644)"], "technique": "album leaf, ink and color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Album leaf", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Overall: 30.2 x 26.7 cm (11 7/8 x 10 1/2 in.)", "dimensions": {"painting only": {"height": 0.246, "height_inch": 9, "height_inch_fraction": 0.6875, "width": 0.227, "width_inch": 8, "width_inch_fraction": 0.9375}, "overall": {"height": 0.302, "height_inch": 11, "height_inch_fraction": 0.875, "width": 0.267, "width_inch": 10, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "Hongshou. \n[seal] Hongshou", "inscription_translation": "Signature and seal of the artist", "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 1}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 304517, "title": "Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</i>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 11-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982); The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (December 3, 1982-February 28, 1983).", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T05:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "CMA, February 11 - March 29, 1981: \"Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting,\" cat. no. 207 pp. 268-272, repr. p. 270, figure 207P", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T00:00:00"}, {"description": "Also to: Kansas City, MO, The Nelson-Atkins Museum, 11/5/80 - 1/4/81", "opening_date": "1980-11-05T00:00:00"}, {"description": "And to: Tokyo, Japan, Tokyo National Museum, 10/4/82 - 11/17/82 as \"Chinese Painting from the Two Distinguished American Museums\"", "opening_date": "1982-10-04T00:00:00"}, {"description": "Approved: Trustees' Minutes 12/18/80", "opening_date": "1980-12-18T00:00:00"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Weng Tonghe \u7fc1\u540c\u9fa2 [1830\u20131904], by descent to  Wango H. C. Weng", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "(Wango H. C. Weng \u7fc1\u842c\u6208 [1918\u20132020], Lyme, NH, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "?\u20131979", "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": [], "date": "1979\u2013", "sortorder": 3}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": ["79.27 o"], "did_you_know": null, "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "The twenty paintings in this double-album by Chen Hongshou include landscapes, figures, and flowers. It also has one leaf featuring a woman, an often-used subject not found in the other albums from the latter part of his career. His late works are wonderful summations of Chen's peculiar and quirky art--archaistic, hyper-refined--but without accompanying shallowness or sentimentality.<br><br>His figures and landscapes in the late albums are miniaturized, not unlike the small Chinese gardens, or the carefully selected small table rocks or old roots used for contemplation to see the world in miniature. This loss of scale is quite deliberate and reflects the psychological situation of a depressed class like the Ming loyalist officials and scholars, deprived of their integrity and honor, and forced to lead a diminished and restricted existence.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60473867"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1979.27.2.16-paintings-after-anci"]}, "citations": [], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1979.27.2.16", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_web.jpg", "width": "794", "height": "900", "filesize": "295629", "filename": "1979.27.2.16_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_print.jpg", "width": "3000", "height": "3400", "filesize": "4507121", "filename": "1979.27.2.16_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_full.tif", "width": "4842", "height": "5488", "filesize": "79743712", "filename": "1979.27.2.16_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "856", "height": "893", "filesize": "514332"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "3258", "height": "3400", "filesize": "8235010"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1979.27.2.16/1979.27.2.16_alt0_full.tif", "width": "5995", "height": "6256", "filesize": "112535232"}, "date_created": "2009-11-10T18:28:11", "annotation": ""}], "creditline": "John L. Severance Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 149621, "creators": [{"id": 6274, "description": "Chen Hongshou (Chinese, 1598/99\u20131652)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": "\u9673\u6d2a\u7dac", "birth_year": "1598", "death_year": "1652", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1979-06-21T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1598, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1598\u20131652", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "component", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": "1979.27", "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-05-29 07:42:24.850000"}, {"id": 153810, "accession_number": "1988.1", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Chinese Beauty (\u5510\u7f8e\u4eba\u56f3), late 1700s\u2013early 1800s. Kubo Shunman (Japanese, 1757\u20131820). Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk; image: 96 x 37 cm (37 13/16 x 14 9/16 in.); overall: 184.2 x 53.3 cm (72 1/2 x 21 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Kelvin Smith Fund, 1988.1", "current_location": null, "title": "Chinese Beauty", "title_in_original_language": "\u5510\u7f8e\u4eba\u56f3", "creation_date": "late 1700s\u2013early 1800s", "creation_date_earliest": 1780, "creation_date_latest": 1820, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["Japan, Edo period (1615\u20131868)"], "technique": "Hanging scroll; ink and color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Japanese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Hanging scroll", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Image: 96 x 37 cm (37 13/16 x 14 9/16 in.); Overall: 184.2 x 53.3 cm (72 1/2 x 21 in.)", "dimensions": {"image": {"height": 0.96, "height_inch": 37, "height_inch_fraction": 0.8125, "width": 0.37, "width_inch": 14, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5625}, "overall": {"height": 1.842, "height_inch": 72, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.533, "width_inch": 21, "width_inch_fraction": 0.0}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 310240, "title": "A Private World: Japanese and Chinese Art from the Kelvin Smith Collection", "description": "<i>A Private World: Japanese and Chinese Art from the Kelvin Smith Collection</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (September 14-November 13, 1988).", "opening_date": "1988-09-14T04:00:00"}, {"id": 211775, "title": "Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art", "description": "<i>Highlights of Asian Paintings from The Cleveland Museum of Art</i>. Nara National Museum (organizer) (February 21-March 29, 1998); Suntory Museum of Art (April 28-June 21, 1998).", "opening_date": "1998-02-21T00:00:00"}, {"id": 202129, "title": "Admired from Afar: Masterworks of Japanese Painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art", "description": "<i>Admired from Afar: Masterworks of Japanese Painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art</i>. Tokyo National Museum, Tokyo, Japan (January 15-February 23, 2014); Kyushu National Museum, Fukuoka, Japan (July 8-August 31, 2014).", "opening_date": "2014-01-15T00:00:00"}, {"id": 440861, "title": "Japan\u2019s Floating World \u65e5\u672c\u306e\u6d6e\u4e16", "description": "<i>Japan\u2019s Floating World \u65e5\u672c\u306e\u6d6e\u4e16</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (organizer) (April 8-October 9, 2022).", "opening_date": "2022-04-08T04:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Japanese Gallery 235 Rotation</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (June 3, 2016\u2013January 10, 2017).", "opening_date": "2016-06-03T00:00:00"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "(Eastern Fine Arts, New York, NY, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131988", "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1988\u2013", "sortorder": 2}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": null, "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "Ukiyo-e artists\u2019 exploration of beautiful people extended to figures from other lands. Here, an elegant Chinese palace lady holding a fan stands before a banana plant. The poem at the top is written in a Japanese appropriation of Chinese called <em>kanbun.</em> Based on its imagery of a palanquin (an enclosed couch with poles used for carrying passengers), silk fan, and autumn winds, it may allude to the story of Lady Ban (about 48 BC\u2013about AD 2). A Chinese beauty famous for her scholarly achievements, Ban was once consort to an emperor but later lost his favor. In a poem attributed to her, she compared herself to a used silk fan put away in autumn.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60476057"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1988.1-chinese-beauty"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "\"The Year in Review for 1988.\" <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 76, no. 2 (1989): 30-75.", "page_number": "Mentioned: no. 205, p. 74; Reproduced: no. 205, p. 59", "url": "www.jstor.org/stable/25160061"}, {"citation": "<em>T\u014dy\u014d kaiga no seika: tokubetsuten: Kur\u012bvurando Bijutsukan no korekushon kara</em> [\u6771\u6d0b\u7d75\u753b\u306e\u7cbe\u83ef : \u7279\u522b\u5c55 : \u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30f4\u30e9\u30f3\u30c8\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306e\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u304b\u3089 = Highlights of Asian painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art]. Japan: Nara National Museum, 1998.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 147, cat. no. 98", "url": null}, {"citation": "<em>Admired from afar: masterworks of Japanese painting from the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> [\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30d6\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u5c55 : \u540d\u753b\u3067\u305f\u3069\u308b\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u7f8e Kur\u012bburando Bijutsukan ten: meiga de tadoru Nihon no bi ]. Tokyo: T\u014dky\u014d Kokuritsu Hakubutsukan, 2014.", "page_number": "Reproduced: cat. no. 21, p. 72", "url": null}, {"citation": "Longhi, Leighton R. <em>Leighton R. Longhi: Forty-Five Years in Asian Art</em>. [New York, N.Y.]: Leighton R. Longhi, 2019.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 317, fig. 315", "url": null}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1988.1", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_web.jpg", "width": "355", "height": "893", "filesize": "70065", "filename": "1988.1_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_print.jpg", "width": "1353", "height": "3400", "filesize": "836634", "filename": "1988.1_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_full.tif", "width": "3094", "height": "7772", "filesize": "72161580", "filename": "1988.1_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "263", "height": "893", "filesize": "45583"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "1002", "height": "3400", "filesize": "530467"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt0_full.tif", "width": "2336", "height": "7924", "filesize": "55553480"}, "date_created": "2013-06-05T15:11:17", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt1_web.jpg", "width": "670", "height": "893", "filesize": "137061"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt1_print.jpg", "width": "2550", "height": "3400", "filesize": "2190398"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt1_full.tif", "width": "6000", "height": "8000", "filesize": "144021692"}, "date_created": "2013-06-05T15:44:59", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt2_web.jpg", "width": "333", "height": "893", "filesize": "244453"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt2_print.jpg", "width": "763", "height": "2048", "filesize": "1250049"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1988.1/1988.1_alt2_full.tif", "width": "763", "height": "2048", "filesize": "4689692"}, "annotation": ""}], "creditline": "Kelvin Smith Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 153810, "creators": [{"id": 65597, "description": "Kubo Shunman (Japanese, 1757\u20131820)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": "\u7aaa \u4fca\u6e80", "birth_year": "1757", "death_year": "1820", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1988-02-18T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1780, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "late 1700s\u2013early 1800s", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "object", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-08-03 14:21:39.654000"}, {"id": 148395, "accession_number": "1976.1", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "In the Palace (\u5bae\u4e2d\u5716), before 1140. After a work attributed to Zhou Wenju (Chinese, active 942\u2013961). Handscroll; ink and light color on silk; painting: 28.5 x 168.6 cm (11 1/4 x 66 3/8 in.); overall: 29.7 x 306.1 cm (11 11/16 x 120 1/2 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1976.1", "current_location": null, "title": "In the Palace", "title_in_original_language": "\u5bae\u4e2d\u5716", "creation_date": "before 1140", "creation_date_earliest": 1127, "creation_date_latest": 1140, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Southern Song dynasty (1127-1279)"], "technique": "Handscroll; ink and light color on silk", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Handscroll", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Painting: 28.5 x 168.6 cm (11 1/4 x 66 3/8 in.); Overall: 29.7 x 306.1 cm (11 11/16 x 120 1/2 in.)", "dimensions": {"painting": {"height": 0.285, "height_inch": 11, "height_inch_fraction": 0.25, "width": 1.686, "width_inch": 66, "width_inch_fraction": 0.375}, "overall": {"height": 0.297, "height_inch": 11, "height_inch_fraction": 0.6875, "width": 3.061, "width_inch": 120, "width_inch_fraction": 0.5}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "1 colophon and 13 seals: 1 colophon and 1 seal of Zheng Cheng \u5f35\u6f82 (d. 1143); 12 seals unidentified.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"inscription": "Colophon by Zhang Cheng \u5f35\u6f82 (d. 1143): \n\n\u5468\u6587\u77e9\u5bae\u4e2d\u5716\u5a66\u4eba\u5c0f\u5152\u5176\u6578\u516b\u5341\uff0c\u4e00\u7537\u5b50\u5beb\u795e\uff0c\u800c\u7ca7\u5177\u3001\u6a02\u5668\u3001\u76c6\u76c2\u3001\u6247\u6905\u5e2d\u3001\u9e1a\u9d61\u3001\u72ac\u8776\u4e0d\u8207\u3002\u6587\u77e9\u53e5\u5bb9\u4eba\uff0c\u70ba\u6c5f\u5357\u7ff0\u6797\u5f85\u8a54\u3002\u4f5c\u58eb\u5973\u9ad4\u8fd1\u5468\u6609\uff0c\u800c\u52a0\u7e96\u9e97\u3002\u5617\u70ba\u5f8c\u4e3b\u756b\u5357\u838a\u5716\uff0c\u865f\u4e00\u6642\u7d55\u7b46\u3002\u5b83\u65e5\u4e0a\u4e4b\u671d\u5ef7\uff0c\u8a54\u7c4d\u4e4b\u7955\u95a3\u3002\u5bae\u4e2d\u5716\u4e91\u662f\u771f\u8e5f\uff0c\u85cf\u524d\u592a\u5e9c\u537f\u6731\u8f09\u5bb6\u3002\u6216\u6479\u4ee5\u898b\u993d\u3002\u5a66\u4eba\u9ad8\u9afb\u81ea\u5510\u4ee5\u4f86\u5982\u6b64\u3002\u6b64\u5377\u8c50\u808c\u9577\u8966\u88d9\uff0c\u5468\u6609\u6cd5\u4e5f\u3002\u4e88\u81f3\u5da0\u5357\uff0c\u65bc\u7aef\u6eaa\u9673\u9ad8\u7956\u4e4b\u88d4\uff0c\u898b\u5176\u4e16\u85cf\u8af8\u5e1d\u50cf\uff0c\u5de6\u53f3\u5bae\u4eba\u68b3\u9afb\u8207\u6b64\u7567\u540c\u3002\u800c\u4e2b\u9b1f\u4e43\u4f5c\u5169\u5927\u9b1f\uff0c\u5782\u80a9\u9805\u9593\uff0c\u96d6\u919c\u800c\u6709\u771f\u614b\u3002\u674e\u6c0f\u81ea\u8b02\u5357\u5510\uff0c\u6545\u8863\u51a0\u591a\u7528\u5510\u5236\uff0c\u7136\u98a8\u6d41\u5bd4\u627f\u516d\u671d\u4e4b\u9918\u3002\u756b\u5bb6\u8005\u8a00\u8fa8\u53e4\u756b\u7576\u5148\u554f\u8863\u51a0\u8eca\u670d\uff0c\u84cb\u8b02\u662f\u4e5f\u3002\u7d39\u8208\u5e9a\u7533\u4e94\u6708\u4e59\u9149\u6fb9\u5d52\u5c45\u58eb\u984c\u3002\n\n\u5370\uff1a\u5f35\u6f82\u5370\u7ae0", "inscription_translation": "[This is] Zhou Wenju\u2019s painting, In the Palace. [In this scroll], women and children number eighty, with a single man. All are drawn to life, not to mention such matters as cosmetic accessories, musical instruments, pots and pans, fans, chairs, mats, parakeets, dogs, and butterflies. Wenju was a native of Jurong. He served as a Hanlin Daizhao [painter-in-waiting] in the south. In figure painting, his style is akin to Zhou Fang\u2019s [active 8th century], but adding a touch of exquisiteness. He once painted a painting titled Southern Villa for Li Houzhu, a painting that was praised at the time as a supreme achievement. In later days, it was presented to the [Song] court and was much cherished in the imperial pavilion [library]. In the Palace was said to be a genuine work by him. It had been in the collection of Zhu Zai, the former Chamberlain for Palace Revenue. Perhaps he had a copy made as a gift, [which is the scroll that I saw]. Women here are depicted with tall chignons, such being the fashion since the Tang dynasty. This scroll presents them with full bodies and also long trailing skirts\u2014this was indeed Zhou Fang\u2019s approach. When in Qiaonan, I visited the descendents of Emperor Gaozu [r. 618\u2013626] of the Chen [dynasty] at Duanxi [near Gaoyao xian, Guangdong province] and saw with my own eyes their family collection of imperial ancestors. The attendant ladies at the sides of these Emperors had the same hairdo as is seen here. The palace servants were shown with two large loops hanging between the neck and shoulder. Although these hairstyles looked ugly, they do appear quite real indeed. The House of Li called its own dynasty Southern Tang; consequently, in matters of fashion, they adhered to the Tang mode. Yet in terms of their cultural origins, they were inheritors of the Six Dynasties. It is the insight of those painters who believed that, in appraising ancient paintings, the first priority lies in the discernment of costumes, furnishings, chariots, and so on. This is indeed the case. On the yiyou day of the fifth moon, the gengshen year of the Shaoxing era, Tanyan Jushi inscribed this. \n\nSeal: \u201cZhang Cheng yin zhang\u201d [seal inadvertently impressed upside down].", "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 2}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 302374, "title": "Year in Review, 1976", "description": "<i>Year in Review, 1976</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (February 1-March 6, 1977).", "opening_date": "1977-02-01T05:00:00"}, {"id": 304517, "title": "Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</i>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 11-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982).", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T05:00:00"}, {"id": 213957, "title": "The Resonance of the Qin in Far Eastern Art", "description": "<i>The Resonance of the Qin in Far Eastern Art</i>. China Institute in America, New York, NY (organizer) (September 16-December 12, 1999).", "opening_date": "1999-09-16T00:00:00"}, {"id": 231365, "title": "Masterpieces of Early Chinese Painting and Calligraphy in American Collections", "description": "<i>Masterpieces of Early Chinese Painting and Calligraphy in American Collections</i>. Shanghai Museum, Shanghai, China (organizer) (November 1, 2012-January 3, 2013).", "opening_date": "2012-11-01T00:00:00"}, {"id": 325382, "title": "The Eternal Feast: Banqueting in 10th-14th Century Chinese Art", "description": "<i>The Eternal Feast: Banqueting in 10th-14th Century Chinese Art</i>. Princeton University Art Museum, Princeton, NJ (organizer) (October 19, 2019-February 16, 2020).", "opening_date": "2019-10-19T04:00:00"}, {"id": 395234, "title": "China\u2019s Southern Paradise: Treasures from the Lower Yangzi Delta", "description": "<i>China\u2019s Southern Paradise: Treasures from the Lower Yangzi Delta</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (September 10, 2023-January 7, 2024).", "opening_date": "2023-09-10T04:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Exhibition of Oriental Art</em>. University Museum, University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, PA (1917, 1922).", "opening_date": "1917-01-01T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>The International Exhibition of Chinese Art</em>. Burlington House, Royal Academy of Arts, London, England (November 28, 1935-March 7, 1936).", "opening_date": "1935-11-01T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Pacific Cultures, China</em>. Golden Gate International Exhibition, San Francisco, CA (1939).", "opening_date": "1939-01-01T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 120)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (January 20-April 22, 2002).", "opening_date": "2002-01-20T05:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 120)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (July 22-October 26, 2003).", "opening_date": "2003-07-22T04:00:00Z"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 120)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (October 19, 2004-April 21, 2005).", "opening_date": "2004-10-19T04:00:00Z"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Zhang Cheng \u5f35\u6f82 [d. 1143]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131143", "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "Shen Zhou \u6c88\u5468 [1427\u20131509]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131509?", "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "(C. T. Loo & Co., New York, NY)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "early 1900s", "sortorder": 3}, {"description": "The University Museum, The University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, PA, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "before 1928\u20131976", "sortorder": 4}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1976\u2013", "sortorder": 5}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "The ladies' elaborate hairstyles, plump figures, and flowing robes are reminiscent of Tang dynasty fashion.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "<em>In the Palace</em> depicts 13 ladies of the imperial household, three servants, and six children in fluent <em>baimiao</em> (plain drawing) brushwork, accentuated by color. The women entertain themselves by making music, tending children, and playing with pets. Their elaborate hairstyles, plump figures, and flowing robes are reminiscent of Tang dynasty <br>fashion. <br><br>The scroll illustrates elegant court life and is a direct copy of the original by Zhou Wenju (active 940\u201375) from Zhenjiang, Jiangsu province. Zhou was employed at the Southern Tang court in Nanjing under Emperor Li Yu (reigned 961\u201376), a prolific poet.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60472972"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1976.1-in-the-palace"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "The CMA handscroll is one part of an original twelfth-century painting, which was divided into four sections. The fourth section is in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.", "page_number": "", "url": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/40004"}, {"citation": "Another section of the handscroll is preserved in the Harvard Art Museums' collection.", "page_number": "", "url": "https://harvardartmuseums.org/collections/object/203790?position=undefined&context=exhibition&id=3251"}, {"citation": "The Bernard Berenson collection at Villa I Tatti, Florence, Italy, also has a section.", "page_number": "", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Fernald, Helen Elizabeth. \"Ladies of the court, an early Chinese scroll painting.\" <em>Museum Journal</em>. v. 19, no. 4 [December 1928], pp. 333\u2013349.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 333\u2013349", "url": null}, {"citation": "<em>The Chinese Exhibition; A Commemorative Catalogue of the International Exhibition of Chinese Art, Royal Academy of Arts, November 1935-March 1936</em>. London: Faber and Faber, 1936.", "page_number": "Mentioned: cat. no. 894, pp. 68, 87", "url": null}, {"citation": "<em>Pacific Cultures, Department of Fine Arts, Division of Pacific Cultures</em>. San Francisco, CA: Golden Gate International Exposition, 1939.", "page_number": "Reproduced: no. 154, pl. N; Mentioned: p. 38", "url": null}, {"citation": "Loehr, Max. \"Chinese Paintings with Sung Dated Inscriptions.\" <em>Ars orientalis: the arts of Islam and the East </em>Volume 4 (1961): 219\u2013284.", "page_number": "Mentioned: p. 252", "url": "https://archive.org/details/arsorientalisart41961univ/page/252"}, {"citation": "Yashiro, Yukio. <em>Nihon bijutsu no saikento\u0304 </em>[Japanese art re-examined = \u65e5\u672c\u7f8e\u8853\u306e\u518d\u691c\u8a0e]. Tokyo: Shincho\u0304sha, 1978.", "page_number": "Reproduced: fig. 102", "url": null}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1978</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1978.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 339", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1978/page/n359"}, {"citation": "Watson, William. <em>L'art de l'ancienne Chine</em>. Paris: Mazenod, 1979.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pl. 41", "url": null}, {"citation": "Ho, Wai-kam, Sherman E. Lee, Laurence Sickman, and Marc F. Wilson. <em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting: The Collections of the Nelson Gallery-Atkins Museum, Kansas City, and the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, in cooperation with Indiana University Press, 1980.", "page_number": "Reproduced: cat. no. 16, pp. 27\u201329", "url": null}, {"citation": "Cunningham, Michael R. \u201cPainting the Poetry of the Natural World.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 75, no. 7 (September 1988): 279\u2013291.", "page_number": "Mentioned and reproduced: p. 281, fig. 2", "url": "http://www.jstor.org/stable/25160039"}, {"citation": "Fu, Shen C. Y. and Jan Stuart. <em>Challenging the Past: The Paintings of Chang Dai-Chien</em>. Washington, D.C.: Arthur M. Sackler Gallery, Smithsonian Institution, 1991.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 150, fig. 82", "url": null}, {"citation": "Addiss, Stephen, Kenneth J. DeWoskin, and Mitchell Clark. <em>The resonance of the qin in East Asian ar</em>t. New York: China Institute Gallery, China Institute, 1999.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pp. 68\u201369, cat. no. 6", "url": null}, {"citation": "Chung, Anita. \"Collaboration and Commemoration: Cleveland's Masterpieces at the Shanghai Museum.\" <em>Orientations </em>43:8 (Nov/Dec 2012): 90\u201395.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pp. 90\u201391, fig. 1", "url": null}, {"citation": "Shanghai bo wu guan. <em>Han mo ju zhen: Zhongguo Riben Meiguo cang Zhongguo gu dai shu hua yi shu</em> [\u7ff0\u58a8\u805a\u73cd: \u4e2d\u570b\u65e5\u672c\u7f8e\u570b\u85cf\u4e2d\u570b\u53e4\u4ee3\u66f8\u756b\u85dd\u8853 = Treasures in the spotlight: art of early Chinese painting and calligraphy in Chinese, Japanese and American collections]. Shanghai Shi: Shanghai shu hua chu ban she, 2012.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pp. 84\u201385, fig. 39", "url": null}, {"citation": "Shanghai bo wu guan. <em>Han mo hui cui: xi du Meiguo cang Zhongguo Wu dai Song Yuan shu hua zhen pin</em> [\u7ff0\u58a8\u8588\u8403: \u7ec6\u8bfb\u7f8e\u56fd\u85cf\u4e2d\u56fd\u4e94\u4ee3\u5b8b\u5143\u4e66\u753b\u73cd\u54c1 = Masterpieces of early Chinese painting and calligraphy in American collections]. Beijing: Beijing da xue chu ban she, 2012.", "page_number": "Mentioned: pp. 329\u2013337, Reproduced: cat no. 39", "url": null}, {"citation": "Chou, Ju-hsi and Anita Chung. <em>Silent poetry: Chinese paintings from the collection of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, 2015.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 44\u201349", "url": null}, {"citation": "Blanchard, Lara C. W. <em>Song Dynasty Figures of Longing and Desire: Gender and Interiority in Chinese Painting and Poetry.</em> Leiden; Boston: Brill, 2018.", "page_number": "Mentioned: pp. 29\u201331, 34, 40; Reproduced: pp. 42\u201345, figs. 2.1- 2.4", "url": null}, {"citation": "Kwok, Zoe S. <em>The Eternal Feast: Banqueting in Chinese Art from the 10th to the 14th Century.</em> Princeton, New Jersey: Princeton University Art Museum, 2019.", "page_number": "Mentioned and reproduced: pp. 131\u2013132, no. 23", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Hu, Luwen. \"From Grassland to Garden-on the Embroidery Nine Goats Heralding the New Year.\" <em>Orientations</em> 50, no. 5 (Sept/Oct 2019): 120\u2013129.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 124", "url": null}, {"citation": "Blanchard, Lara C. W. \"Defining a Female Subjectivity: Gendered Gazes and Feminist Reinterpretations in the Art of Cui Xiuwen and Yu Hong.\" <em>(En)Gendering: Chinese Women's Art in the Making </em>28, no. 1 (February 2020): 177\u2013205.", "page_number": "Mentioned and reproduced: pp. 184\u2013185, fig. 4", "url": ""}, {"citation": "Griswold, William, Xiaofei Tian, Richard Von Glahn, Feng Zhao, S. J. Vainker, Masaaki Itakura, Jiang Wu, et al. <em>China\u2019s Southern Paradise: Treasures from the Lower Yangzi Delta</em>. Edited by Clarissa Von Spee. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 2023.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 139\u2013140, no. 40", "url": ""}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1976.1", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_web.jpg", "width": "900", "height": "87", "filesize": "51121", "filename": "1976.1_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "329", "filesize": "358509", "filename": "1976.1_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_full.tif", "width": "85155", "height": "8237", "filesize": "2104291216", "filename": "1976.1_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "900", "height": "547", "filesize": "99385"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2068", "filesize": "1227445"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1976.1/1976.1_alt0_full.tif", "width": "14204", "height": "8641", "filesize": "368237348"}, "date_created